From d6965ef6d09c3ef7e28f5eca2a01ce10eedd6ba6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ewen <ryan.ewen@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 18:16:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Keep a subagent spawn the transcript primed out of the
 turn-end drain

`SubagentRegistry` doubles as the agentId cache that `getSubagentTranscript`
reads, and `primeFromTranscript` fills it on resume from the Task tool_result
suffixes in the parent transcript. Those records described Tasks that had
already produced a result, but they were written through `recordSpawn`, so
`drainForegroundSpawns` treated every one of them as an in-flight foreground
spawn and dropped it at the end of the next turn, with a warning claiming a
pending spawn had been abandoned.

Two things went with it. The resolver lost its warm cache one turn after
priming it, so reopening a restored subagent chat re-ran the whole strategy
chain. Worse, a background subagent that outlived a host restart has no
`task_started` in the resumed stream to mark its spawn background, so its
record was drained too and the later `system.task_notification` no longer
found a spawn to complete.

Record an agentId learned from a transcript through a separate `cacheAgentId`
entry point that does not claim the spawn is in flight, and drain only spawns
this process saw start.
